    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:</i>&nbsp;<i><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p><b>Manufactured By:</b> The <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Massassi\" title=\"Massassi\">Massassi</a> (<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Species\" title=\"Species\">Species</a>) </p><p><b>Applicable To:</b> Any Armor, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Simple_Weapons_(Melee)\" title=\"Simple Weapons (Melee)\">Simple Weapons (Melee)</a> </p><p>Built by primitive creatures for use in the service of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Sith\" title=\"The Sith\">The Sith</a>, Massassi Manufacture items are designed to take advantage of the strength of their wielders. </p><p><b>Weapons:</b> When a character scores a Critical Hit with a Massassi Weapon held in two hands, that character triples their <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">Strength</a> bonus to damage (before multiplying for the Critical Hit). However, if a character does not have a sufficient <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">Strength</a> score (15 for Medium Weapons, 17 for Large Weapons, or 19 for Huge and bigger weapons) then they take a -2 penalty to attack rolls with that weapon, even if they are proficient with that weapon. </p><p><b>Armors:</b> Massassi Armor allows a Critical Hit against the wearer to be turned into a normal hit once per encounter as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Reaction\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Reaction\">Reaction</a>. However, if a character does not have a sufficient <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">Strength</a> score (13 for <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Light_Armor\" title=\"Light Armor\">Light Armor</a>, 15 for <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medium_Armor\" title=\"Medium Armor\">Medium Armor</a>, or 17 for <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Armor\" title=\"Heavy Armor\">Heavy Armor</a>) they take <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Armor_Check_Penalty\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Armor Check Penalty\">Armor Check Penalties</a> even when proficient in the Armor type. </p>",
